    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1271" name="W1271. DC Inbound Import Container Devanning, Staging &amp; Quality Sampling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import container arrives at DC container yard from port; customs clearance completed per W464
Frequency: ~400–600 TEUs/month across all DCs; ~100–150 containers/DC/month; ~3–5 containers/DC/day
Volume: ~15–25 pallets per container; ~300–500 units per container depending on product category
Owner: DC Receiving Supervisor
Participants: DC Receiving Supervisor, Receiving Clerk, Quality Checker, Putaway Staff, Forklift Operator, Customs Broker (if exception)
Source: workflow W1271 — DC Inbound Import Container Devanning, Staging &amp; Quality Sampling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1271_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1271_Lane1" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1271_Lane2" name="DC Receiving Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1271_Lane3" name="Forklift Operator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1271_Lane4" name="Quality Checker">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1271_Lane5" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1271_Lane6" name="Putaway Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1271_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1271_Start8" name="Import container arrives at DC container yard from port; customs clearance completed per…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task9" name="Container arrival and check-in">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Container arrival and check-in: container chassis arrives at DC container yard from port drayage (W1169); Receiving Clerk verifies: (a) container number matches purchase order and advance shipping notice (ASN), (b) customs seal number matches customs clearance documents per W464, (c) container condition — no visible damage, holes, or water intrusion, (d) container weight matches documented gross weight; Receiving Clerk logs container arrival in system with timestamp
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task10" name="Dock assignment and staging area preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Dock assignment and staging area preparation: DC Receiving Supervisor assigns dock door for devanning based on: (a) container contents — heavy items (tiles, cement) require ground-level dock; lighter items (tools, hardware) can use standard dock, (b) putaway zone proximity — if container contains lumber, assign dock near lumber storage area, (c) current dock availability per W585 (dock scheduling); DC Receiving Supervisor ensures staging area cleared and receiving lane marked for import container
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task11" name="Container positioning and seal breaking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Container positioning and seal breaking: Forklift Operator positions container at assigned dock door; Receiving Clerk and DC Receiving Supervisor jointly: (a) photograph customs seal before breaking, (b) verify seal number against documentation one final time, (c) break seal and open container doors, (d) photograph interior condition immediately after opening — note any shifted pallets, damaged goods, water marks, or pest evidence, (e) if seal discrepancy or visible damage: halt devanning, document with photos, notify customs broker per W464 and Buyer
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / DC Receiving Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task12" name="Devanning (container unloading)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Devanning (container unloading): Forklift Operator and Putaway Staff unload container: (a) palletized goods — forklift removes pallets from container and places in staging lane, (b) floor-loaded goods — manual unloading onto pallets in staging lane, (c) each pallet scanned with RF gun against ASN — system matches item, quantity, and PO line, (d) system flags any quantity discrepancy between ASN and actual count, (e) hazardous materials (paint, solvents, thinners) segregated to designated hazmat staging area per W1222; devanning continues until container fully emptied; target: 45–90 min per container depending on load type
Responsible (R): Forklift Operator / Putaway Staff
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: 45–90 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task13" name="Import quality sampling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Import quality sampling: Quality Checker performs quality sampling per W681 with import-specific checks: (a) Moisture damage check: inspect for water stains, mold, or rust — especially critical for metal goods (rebar, pipes, hardware) and paper-packaged goods (cement, adhesives), (b) Transit damage check: inspect for crushed boxes, broken items, or shifted loads causing damage, (c) Quantity verification: count check against ASN — sample minimum 10% of cartons; if any discrepancy found, expand to 30% or full count, (d) Vendor compliance check: verify labeling, barcoding, and packaging compliance per vendor agreement, (e) AQL sampling: for new vendors or categories, perform AQL (Acceptable Quality Level) inspection per W110 standards; quality results recorded in system with pass/fail and disposition recommendation
Responsible (R): Quality Checker
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: 30–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1271_Task14" name="Landed cost capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Landed cost capture: system automatically calculates landed cost per unit during devanning: (a) product cost (FOB or CIF per PO terms), (b) import duty per customs entry (W464), (c) customs brokerage fees allocated per container, (d) port charges and drayage allocated per container (W1169), (e) marine insurance allocation per W191, (f) DC handling fee estimate; landed cost per unit drives WAC update for inventory valuation — critical for margin accuracy in W102 and W85
Responsible (R): System / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task15" name="Discrepancy resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Discrepancy resolution: if quality or quantity discrepancies found: (a) Quantity shortage: Receiving Clerk logs shortage in system; system adjusts goods receipt to actual count; Buyer notified for vendor claim per W88 (RTV) or debit note, (b) Quantity overage: Receiving Clerk logs overage; Buyer determines — accept (amend PO quantity) or return excess to vendor, (c) Quality failure: Quality Checker logs defect rate and types; disposition options: (i) accept with vendor debit note for defective units, (ii) reject entire shipment — segregate for return per W88, (iii) accept at discounted cost — negotiate vendor credit, (d) all discrepancies documented with photographs for vendor claim evidence per W110
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Quality Checker / Buyer
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: 30–60 min (if discrepancy)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task16" name="Putaway">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Putaway: once quality sampling passed and landed cost captured: (a) system generates putaway assignments per W3 — directing each pallet to optimal bin location based on item velocity and storage requirements, (b) hazardous materials routed to hazmat storage zone per W1222, (c) temperature-sensitive items (adhesives, chemicals) routed to climate-controlled area per W1029, (d) Putaway Staff executes putaway with RF-directed scanning; system updates inventory in real-time
Responsible (R): Putaway Staff
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: Per W3</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1271_Task17" name="Container release and demurrage tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Container release and demurrage tracking: once container fully devanned: (a) Receiving Clerk inspects empty container for any remaining goods or damage, (b) container released to chassis for return to port/container depot, (c) system logs container empty timestamp — tracks total dwell time from arrival to release, (d) if dwell time exceeds free period (typically 5–7 days), system alerts DC Receiving Supervisor and W249 demurrage management workflow activated
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1271_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1271_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1271_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1271_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-250 (ensure controlled execution — DC Inbound Operations (PA-04.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: DC Receiving Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1271_Assoc20" sourceRef="W1271_Annotation19" targetRef="W1271_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1271_Flow21" sourceRef="W1271_Start8" targetRef="W1271_Task9" />
