    <bpmn:process id="W_W1279" name="W1279. DC Cross-Dock Fast-Mover Processing &amp; Direct Putaway to Outbound" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Inbound shipment of fast-moving A-class items (cement, nails, paint) where DC acts as flow-through rather than storage node
Frequency: Daily; ~30–40% of inbound volume for A-class SKUs
Volume: ~1,200–1,600 cross-dock pallet positions/month across 4 DCs
Owner: DC Operations Supervisor
Participants: DC Receiving Lead, DC Dispatch, Supply Planner, Transportation Coordinator
Source: workflow W1279 — DC Cross-Dock Fast-Mover Processing &amp; Direct Putaway to Outbound</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1279_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1279_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1279_Lane2" name="DC Dispatch">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1279_Lane3" name="DC Receiving Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1279_Lane4" name="DC Warehouse Crew">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1279_Lane5" name="DC Operations Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1279_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1279_Start7" name="Inbound shipment of fast-moving A-class items (cement, nails, paint) where DC acts as…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1279_Task8" name="Cross-dock eligibility flag">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Cross-dock eligibility flag: Supply Planner or system identifies inbound PO lines eligible for cross-dock based on: (a) ABC classification = A, (b) active store replenishment orders exist for the item, (c) inbound quantity ≤ sum of open replenishment quantities (no excess requiring storage), (d) item does not require quality inspection hold per W681
Responsible (R): System / Supply Planner
Accountable (A): DC Operations Supervisor
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1279_Task9" name="Inbound-outbound matching">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inbound-outbound matching: System matches cross-dock-eligible inbound lines to pending store replenishment orders; generates cross-dock allocation plan: (a) inbound PO line → outbound delivery assignment, (b) pallet-level allocation to specific stores, (c) outbound truck loading sequence based on delivery route per W196
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): DC Operations Supervisor
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1279_Task10" name="Pre-staging outbound trucks">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pre-staging outbound trucks: DC Dispatch pre-positions outbound trailers at designated cross-dock doors; confirms truck readiness (clean, no residual cargo, correct vehicle for route); DC Receiving Lead assigns dedicated cross-dock receiving lane with direct sightline to outbound dock
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch / DC Receiving Lead
Accountable (A): DC Operations Supervisor
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1279_Task11" name="Rapid receiving &amp; quality check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Rapid receiving &amp; quality check: Inbound truck arrives; DC Receiving Lead performs expedited receiving: (a) scan ASN barcode per W1365, (b) visual quality inspection (no visible damage, correct packaging), (c) pallet count verification against ASN; for cross-dock A-items, quality sampling reduced to 5% (vs. the standard 10% sampling per W1600) based on historical vendor quality score per W44
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Lead
Accountable (A): DC Operations Supervisor
Duration: 30–60 min/truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1279_Task12" name="Direct transfer to outbound">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Direct transfer to outbound: Goods moved directly from inbound dock to outbound dock via forklift or pallet jack; each pallet scanned and system confirms store assignment; pallet labeled with store-specific routing label; system updates inventory in real-time as goods move through DC without putaway
Responsible (R): DC Warehouse Crew
Accountable (A): DC Operations Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min/truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1279_Task13" name="Outbound dispatch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Outbound dispatch: Once all cross-dock pallets loaded onto outbound truck, DC Dispatch completes dispatch per W196; system generates delivery manifest; truck departs for store delivery; inventory records show goods receipt and goods issue in same transaction batch
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch
Accountable (A): DC Operations Supervisor
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1279_Task14" name="Daily cross-dock performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Daily cross-dock performance tracking: DC Operations Supervisor reviews daily cross-dock metrics: (a) cross-dock throughput (pallets/hour), (b) dock-to-stock time (target: &lt;4 hours from inbound arrival to outbound dispatch), (c) cross-dock accuracy (correct store allocation), (d) exceptions requiring putaway (inbound qty exceeded replenishment demand)
Responsible (R): DC Operations Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1279_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1279_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1279_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1279_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-250 (ensure controlled execution — DC Inbound Operations (PA-04.1).) | - operational: restricting cross-dock to high-reliability vendors (quality score &gt;95% per W44)
Owner: DC Operations Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
