    <bpmn:process id="W_W1307" name="W1307. DC Cross-Dock Fast-Mover Expedited Receiving, Sortation &amp; Same-Day Dispatch Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Inbound shipment arrives at DC containing pre-identified cross-dock items (fast-movers, promotional stock, urgent replenishment)
Frequency: Daily at each DC; ~30–40% of inbound volume flows through cross-dock
Volume: ~10–15 cross-dock pallets/containers per DC per day; ~1,200–1,600 cross-dock pallet positions/month chain-wide (per W1279)
Owner: DC Operations Manager
Participants: DC Receiving Lead, Cross-Dock Sortation Team, DC Dispatch Coordinator, Transportation Planner
Source: workflow W1307 — DC Cross-Dock Fast-Mover Expedited Receiving, Sortation &amp; Same-Day Dispatch Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1307_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1307_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1307_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1307_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1307_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1307_Lane2" name="DC Receiving Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1307_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1307_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1307_Lane3" name="DC Dispatch Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1307_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1307_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1307_Start5" name="Inbound shipment arrives at DC containing pre-identified cross-dock items (fast-movers…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1307_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1307_Task6" name="Pre-arrival cross-dock planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-arrival cross-dock planning: (a) before inbound shipment arrival: system identifies cross-dock eligible items from the inbound ASN: (i) items flagged as cross-dock in item master (A-class, fast-mover designation), (ii) items on store replenishment order backorder (urgency flag), (iii) promotional items with upcoming sale event dates; (b) system generates cross-dock sort plan: (i) item × quantity × destination store, (ii) assign to outbound delivery routes departing same day, (iii) allocate dock door for cross-dock staging (separate from standard receiving dock); (c) Cross-Dock Sortation Team receives sort plan on handheld devices before truck arrival
Responsible (R): System / DC Receiving Lead
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 30–60 min before arrival</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1307_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1307_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1307_Task7" name="Expedited receiving &amp; sortation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Expedited receiving &amp; sortation: (a) inbound truck arrives at designated cross-dock door; (b) DC Receiving Lead performs rapid receiving: (i) scan ASN barcode on pallet/case — system confirms item is cross-dock eligible, (ii) verify quantity against ASN (tolerance: ± 2% for case count), (iii) quick quality check: packaging intact, no visible damage, correct labeling — full QC deferred for cross-dock (performed on exception basis); (c) Cross-Dock Sortation Team immediately sorts received items: (i) scan item barcode → system displays destination store and outbound route, (ii) place item in store-labeled staging lane on dock (each lane corresponds to a store delivery route), (iii) system tracks sortation progress in real-time; (d) target: from truck arrival to sortation complete = 60–90 minutes for a full truck
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Lead / Cross-Dock Sortation Team
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 60–90 min per truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1307_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1307_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1307_Task8" name="Same-day dispatch &amp; loadout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Same-day dispatch &amp; loadout: (a) as sortation completes for each outbound route: DC Dispatch Coordinator stages outbound truck: (i) load cross-docked items onto delivery truck in reverse-stop sequence (last store loaded first), (ii) combine cross-docked items with standard warehouse-picked items for the same route, (iii) generate load manifest with all items (cross-dock + standard) per route; (b) cross-dock items received before 10:00 AM dispatched same day on afternoon delivery routes; (c) cross-dock items received after 10:00 AM dispatched next morning; (d) system updates inventory status: cross-dock items move from &quot;In Transit to DC&quot; directly to &quot;In Transit to Store&quot; (bypassing &quot;In DC&quot; status)
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch Coordinator / Transportation Planner
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per route</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1307_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1307_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1307_Task9" name="Cross-dock exception handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-dock exception handling: (a) Overshipment: vendor ships more than ordered → excess received into standard putaway (not cross-docked), vendor notified per W109; (b) Quality failure: quick check reveals damaged or wrong items → failed items pulled from cross-dock, received into standard receiving for QC hold per W1225, replacement sourced from DC stock if available; (c) Missing store allocation: item received but no open replenishment order for any store → received into standard putaway (converts from cross-dock to stock); (d) Sortation error: item placed in wrong store lane → discovered at loadout when scanning item to manifest, corrected to correct lane; if discovered after dispatch: receiving store processes transfer per W219 to correct store
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Lead
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: Per exception: 10–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1307_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1307_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1307_Task10" name="Daily cross-dock performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Daily cross-dock performance tracking: (a) system tracks daily cross-dock KPIs: (i) cross-dock volume as % of total inbound, (ii) average dock-to-dispatch time (target: &lt; 4 hours), (iii) same-day dispatch rate (target: ≥ 80% of cross-dock items dispatched same day), (iv) sortation accuracy (target: ≥ 99.5%), (v) exception rate (target: &lt; 5%); (b) DC Operations Manager reviews daily KPIs and addresses bottlenecks; (c) weekly: compare cross-dock performance across 4 DCs — identify and replicate best practices from top-performing DC
Responsible (R): System / DC Operations Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1307_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1307_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1307_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1307_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1307_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-250 (ensure controlled execution — DC Inbound Operations (PA-04.1).) | - operational: DC Operations Manager review and approval gate
Owner: DC Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1307_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1307_Annotation12" targetRef="W1307_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1307_Flow14" sourceRef="W1307_Start5" targetRef="W1307_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1307_Flow15" sourceRef="W1307_Task6" targetRef="W1307_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1307_Flow16" sourceRef="W1307_Task7" targetRef="W1307_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1307_Flow17" sourceRef="W1307_Task8" targetRef="W1307_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1307_Flow18" sourceRef="W1307_Task9" targetRef="W1307_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1307_Flow19" sourceRef="W1307_Task10" targetRef="W1307_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1307_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1307_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1307">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1307_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1307_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
