    <bpmn:process id="W_W1365" name="W1365. DC Inbound Vendor ASN Pre-Receipt Verification &amp; PO Matching Exception Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor submits Advance Shipping Notice (ASN) via vendor portal or EDI for an incoming shipment
Frequency: ~6,000 DC goods receipts/month across 4 DCs (the goods-receipt canon); portal-enabled vendors account for ~80% of receipt volume, with ASN pre-notification riding the PO spine — ~700–750 ASNs/month, ~60% of the ~1,200 merchandise POs (per W1006; ~40% of vendors by count lack access — see pain points)
Volume: ~700–750 ASN submissions/month (1 ASN per PO per W1006 — the ASN spine is the ~1,200-merchandise-PO universe, not the ~6,000-receipt universe; a PO delivered across multiple partial truck receipts carries one ASN); ~15–20% have discrepancies requiring exception handling = ~105–150 exceptions/month
Owner: DC Inbound Supervisor
Participants: DC Inbound Supervisor, Receiving Clerk, Buyer, Vendor (via portal), Import Coordinator (for import shipments)
Source: workflow W1365 — DC Inbound Vendor ASN Pre-Receipt Verification &amp; PO Matching Exception Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1365_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1365_Lane1" name="Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1365_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1365_Lane3" name="DC Inbound Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1365_Lane4" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1365_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1365_Start6" name="Vendor submits Advance Shipping Notice (ASN) via vendor portal or EDI for an incoming…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1365_Task7" name="Vendor submits ASN via vendor portal: PO reference, SKU list with quantities…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor submits ASN via vendor portal: PO reference, SKU list with quantities, expected delivery date, carrier, and number of pallets/cases
Responsible (R): Vendor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Vendor-initiated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1365_Task8" name="System auto-matches ASN to open PO: verifies PO number exists, PO status is…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System auto-matches ASN to open PO: verifies PO number exists, PO status is &quot;Open&quot; (not cancelled or closed), SKU numbers match PO lines, quantities are within PO tolerance (+/- 10%)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1365_Task9" name="If full match: system pre-assigns dock door, generates pre-receipt record with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: If full match: system pre-assigns dock door, generates pre-receipt record with expected items; Receiving Clerk proceeds to rapid scan-based receiving upon truck arrival
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1365_Task10" name="If partial match or mismatch: system creates exception record with discrepancy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If partial match or mismatch: system creates exception record with discrepancy details (wrong SKU, quantity overage/shortage, PO not found, PO closed); routes to DC Inbound Supervisor
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1365_Task11" name="DC Inbound Supervisor reviews exception: determines resolution — (a) accept…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: DC Inbound Supervisor reviews exception: determines resolution — (a) accept shipment with PO amendment by Buyer, (b) accept partial shipment (only matched lines), (c) reject entire shipment, or (d) hold shipment pending vendor clarification
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 10–20 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1365_Task12" name="For resolution (a): Supervisor contacts Buyer to create PO amendment or new PO…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: For resolution (a): Supervisor contacts Buyer to create PO amendment or new PO; Buyer approves or rejects based on current demand
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1365_Task13" name="For resolution (d): Supervisor contacts vendor via portal messaging; vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: For resolution (d): Supervisor contacts vendor via portal messaging; vendor provides corrected ASN or explanation; system matches corrected ASN to PO
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor / Vendor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1365_Task14" name="Weekly: DC Inbound Supervisor produces ASN accuracy report by vendor; vendors…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly: DC Inbound Supervisor produces ASN accuracy report by vendor; vendors with &lt; 70% ASN accuracy are flagged for Vendor Performance review (W26)
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1365_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1365_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1365_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1365_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-250 (ensure controlled execution — DC Inbound Operations (PA-04.1).) | - operational: DC Inbound Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: DC Inbound Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
