    <bpmn:process id="W_W1366" name="W1366. DC Inbound Damage Claim Processing, Vendor Chargeback &amp; Freight Recovery Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Receiving Clerk identifies damaged goods during DC inbound receiving inspection (W3, W681)
Frequency: ~2–3% of inbound shipments have some damage = ~120–180 damage incidents/month across 4 DCs
Volume: ~120–180 incidents/month; damage value ranges from PHP 5,000 (minor carton damage) to PHP 500,000+ (full container of shattered tiles)
Owner: DC Inbound Supervisor
Participants: DC Inbound Supervisor, Receiving Clerk, Buyer, Finance (AP/AR), Vendor, Freight Carrier/Forwarder, Import Coordinator (for import shipments)
Source: workflow W1366 — DC Inbound Damage Claim Processing, Vendor Chargeback &amp; Freight Recovery Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1366_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1366_Lane1" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1366_Lane2" name="DC Inbound Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1366_Lane3" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1366_Lane4" name="Finance (AP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1366_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1366_Start6" name="Receiving Clerk identifies damaged goods during DC inbound receiving inspection (W3, W681)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task7" name="Receiving Clerk identifies damaged goods during receiving inspection…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Receiving Clerk identifies damaged goods during receiving inspection: photographs damage (multiple angles), records damaged SKU, quantity, and damage type (crushed, water-damaged, broken, scratched, missing parts) on receiving exception report
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Inbound Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task8" name="DC Inbound Supervisor assesses damage severity: minor (salvageable at…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: DC Inbound Supervisor assesses damage severity: minor (salvageable at discount), moderate (usable with rework), or total loss; determines responsible party based on damage pattern and transit chain
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task9" name="Supervisor segregates damaged goods to designated damage staging area; updates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Supervisor segregates damaged goods to designated damage staging area; updates inventory status to &quot;damaged/hold&quot; in system to prevent allocation to store orders
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task10" name="For vendor-caused damage (packaging failure, manufacturing defect): Supervisor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For vendor-caused damage (packaging failure, manufacturing defect): Supervisor creates vendor chargeback in system with photo evidence; chargeback amount deducted from next vendor payment via AP (W7)
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor
Accountable (A): Buyer
Duration: 15–20 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task11" name="For carrier-caused damage (transit damage): Supervisor creates carrier claim…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For carrier-caused damage (transit damage): Supervisor creates carrier claim with supporting documentation (delivery receipt noting damage, photos, commercial invoice value); submits claim to carrier within 48 hours per carrier contract terms
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 20–30 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task12" name="For import container damage (condensation, shifting): Import Coordinator files…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: For import container damage (condensation, shifting): Import Coordinator files claim with marine insurance provider; provides survey report, photos, and cargo manifest
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task13" name="Finance processes approved chargebacks: vendor chargeback offset against open…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Finance processes approved chargebacks: vendor chargeback offset against open AP; carrier claim recovery recorded as other income; insurance claim recovery recorded upon settlement; unrecoverable damage written off as inventory shrinkage
Responsible (R): Finance (AP/AR)
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 15 min/claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1366_Task14" name="Monthly: DC Inbound Supervisor produces damage analysis report: damage rate by…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly: DC Inbound Supervisor produces damage analysis report: damage rate by vendor, by carrier, by product category, and by damage type; high-damage vendors flagged for Vendor Performance review (W26) and packaging improvement requirements
Responsible (R): DC Inbound Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1366_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1366_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1366_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1366_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-250 (ensure controlled execution — DC Inbound Operations (PA-04.1).) | - operational: DC Inbound Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: DC Inbound Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
